<dtmi:dtdl:class:SemanticType;4> <http://azure.com/DigitalTwins/MetaModel/dtdlVersion> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<dtmi:dtdl:class:SemanticType;4> <http://azure.com/DigitalTwins/MetaModel/remarks> "As a practical matter, usage of the extensible classes is not affected by this lack of hierarchical relationship:" .
<dtmi:dtdl:class:SemanticType;4> <http://azure.com/DigitalTwins/MetaModel/remarks> "Extension types that are semantic inherit from SemanticType; extension types that are not semantic inherit from other types." .
<dtmi:dtdl:class:SemanticType;4> <http://azure.com/DigitalTwins/MetaModel/remarks> "Future versions of the metaparser might support either hierarchically related extensible classes or extensibility differences across language versions, but the DTDL v3 parser does not." .
<dtmi:dtdl:class:SemanticType;4> <http://azure.com/DigitalTwins/MetaModel/remarks> "In particular, both AdjunctType and SemanticType are dtmm:Extensible, so subclassing would create a hierarichal relationship between two extensible classes in the metamodel." .
<dtmi:dtdl:class:SemanticType;4> <http://azure.com/DigitalTwins/MetaModel/remarks> "Intuitively, SemanticType should be a subclass of AdjunctType; however, there are implementation challenges with making it so." .
<dtmi:dtdl:class:SemanticType;4> <http://azure.com/DigitalTwins/MetaModel/remarks> "Theoretically, the dtmm:Extensible type could be removed from SemanticType;4, but since it is present on SemanticType;2, extensibility would differ across language versions." .
<dtmi:dtdl:class:SemanticType;4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://azure.com/DigitalTwins/MetaModel/Abstract> .
<dtmi:dtdl:class:SemanticType;4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://azure.com/DigitalTwins/MetaModel/Extensible> .
