<dtmi:dtdl:class:Unit;4> <http://azure.com/DigitalTwins/MetaModel/remarks> "As a practical matter, usage of the extensible classes is not affected by this lack of hierarchical relationship:" .
<dtmi:dtdl:class:Unit;4> <http://azure.com/DigitalTwins/MetaModel/remarks> "Future versions of the metaparser might support either hierarchically related extensible classes or extensibility differences across language versions, but the DTDL v3 parser does not." .
<dtmi:dtdl:class:Unit;4> <http://azure.com/DigitalTwins/MetaModel/remarks> "In particular, both LatentType and Unit are dtmm:Extensible, so subclassing would create a hierarichal relationship between two extensible classes in the metamodel." .
<dtmi:dtdl:class:Unit;4> <http://azure.com/DigitalTwins/MetaModel/remarks> "Intuitively, Unit should be a subclass of LatentType, not of Entity; however, there are implementation challenges with making it so." .
<dtmi:dtdl:class:Unit;4> <http://azure.com/DigitalTwins/MetaModel/remarks> "Latent types that are units inherit from Unit; latent types that are not units inherit from other types." .
<dtmi:dtdl:class:Unit;4> <http://azure.com/DigitalTwins/MetaModel/remarks> "Theoretically, the dtmm:Extensible type could be removed from Unit;4, but since it is present on Unit;2, extensibility would differ across language versions." .
